A cozy living room rendered in Vincent van Gogh's swirling, expressive brushstroke style, featuring two young twin boys lying on their stomachs on a vibrant carpet, completely absorbed in building an elaborate wooden block tower together. The room glows with warm amber and golden yellows, with bold impasto textures creating movement in the walls and furniture. Where a television would typically sit, there is instead a large window with swirling starry-night-inspired curtains billowing open, revealing a lush garden beckoning outside. Scattered around the children are picture books, crayons, and toy dinosaurs. The empty TV cabinet has been transformed into a bookshelf overflowing with colorful spines. Evening light streams through the window in characteristic Van Gogh spiraling rays, casting dancing shadows across the scene. The entire composition radiates warmth, imagination, and the intimate energy of childhood discovery.
